1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
When peak electrical demand stresses the municipal grid, EchoGrid incentivizes residents

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
to shed heavy inductive appliance load without expensive smart meters.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Users connect a non-custodial Stellar wallet or generate a temporary in-browser keypair

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:22,000
funded instantly via Friendbot on Stellar Testnet.

5
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Using pure in-browser DSP via Web Audio API and Web Workers, EchoGrid's Edge detector

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:38,000
listens for the characteristic acoustic hum of heavy motors and air conditioners. Audio never leaves the device.

7
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:44,000
When the appliance powers off, our streaming detector recognizes the sudden drop in mains frequency harmonics

8
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:50,000
and immediately constructs a cryptographic proof of power-down.

9
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:57,000
The proof is verified by the live Rust oracle against a time-bound challenge nonce.

10
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:05,000
The Soroban escrow contract executes an automated micropayment bounty on Stellar Testnet within seconds.

11
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:18,000
The EchoGrid MVP trusts the client's claim of an appliance power-down. While cryptographic challenge nonces, recipient cooldowns, and on-chain spending caps strictly limit potential abuse, they do not prove that an appliance physically turned off. This live demonstration showcases the end-to-end micropayment loop and real-time acoustic detection user experience on Stellar Testnet; physical and cryptographic verification remains post-MVP work.
